WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.801
-Welcome back to the show.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.067
-You recently bought an
apartment in New York City.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.434
-I did.
It's not great, though.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.734
-It's not that great, yeah.
It's very interesting.

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:09.934
You bought my old apartment.
-I did.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.467
Yes, I live in your --
I live in your house.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.133
I sleep in your bed.
Is that weird?

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.467
-That's not weird at all.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.501
I'm just --
How do you like it?

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.701
You just moved in,
just happened.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.167
-It's one of the most
incredible places

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:22.567
that I've ever lived in,
obviously.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.968
But, I just --
I can't believe it.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.701
I feel so connected to you,
but I feel so grateful, man.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.601
-I'm so grateful --
-'Cause you lived in that

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:29.901
apartment since
you were how old?

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.601
-I was probably 20 years old.
-You could smell it.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.801
-You could smell it, yeah.
I'm just so happy

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.501
because when you sell
an apartment,

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.767
you're like,
"I hope someone cool buys it

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.300
and someone creative buys it,
and someone loving buys it,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.133
and you fit all those --
check all those boxes.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.767
'Cause all the little bits,
and I never --

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.667
I didn't want to change anything
about this house, honestly.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.567
I tried to design my house
in L.A. basically like that

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.534
without knowing the house.
Like, this house is what I

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.868
would've designed if
I had style, basically.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.567
His wife, Nancy -- I mean,
the whole place is beautiful.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:01:00.167
-It's all my wife, yeah.
-Love you, Nancy!

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:03.501
-We have old wallpaper --
-I kept it all. It's creepy.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.701
-No, I love it.
We're like, "Thank you,

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.067
thank you, thank you.
'Cause we worked so hard on it."

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.767
I'm like, "Please don't just
paint it all, and..."

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.267
-Kept the bed sheets,
everything.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.501
-I love you, buddy.
I'm so happy that it's you.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.434
I'm so happy that it's you.
I love you.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:17.801
-Welcome any time.
-Yeah. I want --

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.734
I wanted to ask you about
this thing.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.601
I saw Megan Thee Stallion...
-Yes.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:22.934
-...at the
Billboard Music Awards.

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:24.968
-So did I.
-Yeah, you did too, apparently.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.868
-I was there.
-No one understood

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.367
what was happening
because you weren't quite --

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.634
you weren't quite at the awards
nor were with her.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.100
You were off to the side.
-Yes.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.467
-And if you can't even --
If you don't even look at that,

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.667
there's Megan Thee Stallion.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.467
-You see Megan.
And then off to the side...

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.033
-Peekaboo!
-...that's you, yeah.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.634
[ Laughter ]
And what's going on?

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.100
How did you end up here?
-So, basically, I was kind of

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.300
working as her P.A.
I needed a side job.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.634
Um, no, but, basically,
you know, I was in Vegas.

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.567
We're friends.
I really wanted to see her play,

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.000
and she asked me
to come along with her,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.567
and I was like --
I didn't know I was gonna go

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.434
and sit or do anything.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:59.367
I thought I was just gonna come
and watch her play.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.567
You know, she had a speech
she was gonna do,

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.100
'cause she was winning an award.
I was helping her run her lines.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.367
Like, I was walking around
with a clipboard,

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.300
helping her do lines.
-Yeah, you were like

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.367
an assistant, yeah.
-Memorize the speech.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.834
And, you know,
so she was on the red carpet.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.534
So I was standing behind her,
and then she was trying to --

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.834
You know, the thing with
fashion, you try

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.234
and flick your own thing,
and she couldn't really --

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.100
So I was helping her,
and I was doing it,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.567
and going like, "Yeah, go!"
Like, hyping her up.

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:21.200
Being a hype woman.
-Yeah. You flipped her scarf,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.667
and then you were like,
"Yeah! Go get 'em! Go!"

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, and then, like,

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:28.334
I walked in, and I had a seat
in the front row.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.167
I'm like,
"I'm not meant to be here."

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.334
So I was like, "Hi!"
And then, like, I was

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.734
getting on the floor,
taking pictures.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.100
That's what I do.
I don't know.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.000
I was just really excited.
"Let me get an angle, guys!

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.868
I'm a photographer."
-It was so fun.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.300
I'm like, "I have no idea.
I know Cara, but I don't know

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.567
what she's doing."
-I was living my best life,

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:42.701
but people found it
a little bit odd, which I --

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.434
People find me odd,
but that's me.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.033
-Yeah, why not?
-No shame.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.734
-I love you in
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:49.834
-Thank you.
-Which is one of

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.167
my favorite shows.
On Hulu.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.334
-It's one of my favorite shows,
too, and I'm in it.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.767
That's weird.
-Selena Gomez, Steve Martin,

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.267
Martin Short.
-Yes.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:58.868
-How was it like?
How did you know that you were

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.167
being added to the cast,
by the way?

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.467
Did you get a call,
and they go, like --

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.868
yeah, they go,
"Oh, we want you to play..."

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.901
-Well, the weird thing was,
I just finished a show.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.367
I just finished "Carnival Row,"
and I was like --

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.100
I think I needed
a break for a little bit,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.234
'cause I'd done this show for
like coming up

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.601
to four years, eight months.
And, like, I don't know.

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:17.467
My agent called me up and said,
"So, they've asked you

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.467
to be in this show."
And I was like,

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.968
"Oh, she's probably joking."
Because, also, I hadn't met

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.334
the director or anything,
and they were just like,

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.567
"They want you to be in it,"
and I was like,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.400
"If this is a joke,
I'm gonna be so angry.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.434
But if this isn't, I'll pay."
And she was like,

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.567
"You shouldn't say that
to people."

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.400
[ Laughter ]
-"I will pay you

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.901
to be in this show, 'cause..."
-And then they're like,

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:36.167
"You play a queer, English,
wannabe artist."

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.634
I was like, "Okay.
That sounds odd."

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:39.801
[ Laughter ]
"Never done that before."

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.667
-I love
that you're in there.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:44.400
How is Steve and Marty
to deal with?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.667
I know they're kind of
nightmares.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.133
-Pretty rough, man, yeah.
-Yeah, they're nightmares.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.667
-I have to teach them
a few things about comedy.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.000
-Yeah, good for you,
Yeah, please, yeah.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.934
-No, I mean, honestly,
they are my heroes.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:55.801
I grew up watching them.
My dad was so happy.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.601
I just --
But the thing is,

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.634
coming into a new show
and you haven't been

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.601
in the first season,
just not really part,

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:04.701
but straight away, I was --
Marty took me in, he was like,

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.601
"I want to see --
Let's get to know you."

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.367
We were talking about what
our favorite condiments were,

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:11.067
what my thoughts on family,
kind of grilled me a little bit.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:13.534
But I felt so a part of it.
-Do you see that you're more

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.467
of a Martin Short person
or more of Steve person?

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.868
-No, no, Selena is Steve,
and I'm Marty, for sure.

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.734
Like, it's -- they're kind of
both looking out,

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:22.367
and we're trying to do...
[ Singing ]

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.834
Like, singing,
and Steve and Selena are like,

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:27.567
"Guys, can we please just
get on with this thing?"

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.567
-I have a picture here of --
just a picture.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.868
This is a random day on set.
-Random day on set.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.400
-No big deal.
Yeah, just you guys hanging out.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.634
And then, look at that.
Yeah.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:38.334
Steven Spielberg
just dropped by.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.634
Steven Spielberg
just drops by the set.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.133
-And I think he must have
mentioned it,

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.801
but I don't know if he --
He was just like,

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.634
"Oh, yeah, guys, my friend
Steven's coming along."

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:46.901
"Yeah, yeah, cool, cool.
And then he walked in,

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.767
we're like, "What the hell?"
-"Wait.

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.467
That's your friend, Steven?"
-Steven Spielberg.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.267
You could've mentioned that,
maybe.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:57.534
-Look at Steve and Marty.
-He was such a big fan

00:04:57.534 --> 00:04:58.968
of the show, and it was so nice,

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.367
'cause he was asking
all these questions.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.834
-Look at Steve Martin.
It's unbelievably funny.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:10.801
Oh, my gosh.
-No, I don't wish anyone else --

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.067
-Casual, casual fans.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.501
-I do want
to show everyone a clip.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:16.367
Here's Cara Delevingne in
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:17.934
We don't know
if you're the murderer or not.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.167
We don't know anything.
-Nobody knows.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.167
-It's a mystery.
Check it out.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:24.367
-Want to show you something.
I've been hideously blocked

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:28.100
for a year, stuck in the past,
no moving forward.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.167
Do you ever feel that way?
-Yeah, all the time.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.767
-Stupid question.
Of course you do.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.968
Anyway, then this happened.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:43.033
♪♪

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:46.334
-Wow.
It's beautiful.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:49.400
-I'm glad you like it.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.400
'Cause it's you.

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:59.501
And I want you to destroy it.

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.434
-That is so --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.567
Fashion, art.
Wow.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:08.234
-Art.
-"Destroy it."

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:09.801
Cara, every time
you've been on the show,

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.367
you've been nice,
very nice to us.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.200
You've shown us
some secret, hidden talents.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.567
You beatboxed
on our show before.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.100
-Yes.
-Do you remember that?

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.667
You played electric guitar
behind your head.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:18.968
And you crushed with that.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.667
And tonight,
you've brought us a magic trick.

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:24.267
-I have.
So I call myself

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:26.701
a bit of a "vagician," I'll say.

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.501
Look at my earring.
-Okay.

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.601
All right.
Not a magician.

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:35.133
-Not a magician.
Vagician.

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:37.300
So I've got a pack of cards
here, okay?

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.167
This might not go well.
That's all I'm gonna tell you.

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:41.434
'Cause my hands are
a little sweaty.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.267
-Do you know the trick?
-I don't know.

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:47.400
My hands are a little sweaty.
And I'm a little nervous.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.901
So this is gonna go really well,
I promise you.

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.467
-Okay. All right.
-So I'm gonna shuffle the cards.

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:51.634
-I'm not looking.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:53.968
-If it doesn't go well,
please forgive me.

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.767
-We'll be fine.
We're on your side.

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:58.334
We're on your side.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.267
-So, I've shuffled the cards.

00:07:00.267 --> 00:07:04.000
I've shuffled the cards.
So, I've shuffled the cards.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.334
So I've shuffled the cards.
I'm gonna run through the cards.

00:07:06.334 --> 00:07:07.734
Yeah, this is perfect,
perfect, perfect, perfect.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.033
Give me some light, yeah, yeah.

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:11.400
I've shuffled the cards,
and now I'm gonna

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.167
shuffle through the cards,
and you're gonna tell me to stop

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:15.601
whenever you want me to stop.
Tell me to stop.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.901
-Stop.
-Okay.

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:20.000
So, this is your card.
I'm not going to look at it.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.467
-Yes, I see it.
-I'm gonna put it to the camera.

00:07:22.467 --> 00:07:24.167
Also not gonna look.
-Can we all see it?

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:25.234
-Yeah?
-All right, good.

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:26.267
We all see it.
-Can you see how much

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:27.534
my hand is shaking?
-Yes.

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:28.734
[ Laughter ]
Is that part of the trick?

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.601
-Okay, so now I'm gonna
put the card there.

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.200
Right?
This is the card, right?

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.000
Yeah, that was the card.
I know what I'm doing.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.200
-This is like --
-So, before we forget about --

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.067
we forget about that now.
So close your eyes.

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:41.701
[ Laughter ]
No, I'm joking.

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.200
So, as --
no, close your eyes.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.367
Oh, I thought you were joking.
-Also, I just wanted to get you

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.968
a little present as a thank-you
for letting me be in your house.

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.400
This is a bottle of Prosecco.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.834
But now I'm gonna ask you
a question.

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:52.767
You're gonna have to guess --
You can open your eyes now.

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:55.467
This is a bottle of Prosecco.
-Why did I close my eyes?

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.400
-I also happen to own
the company with my sister.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.934
-Why did you have me
close my eyes?

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:01.934
-Because I wanted you to be
surprised by the present.

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.734
-Thank you!
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:06.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.267
-This is not a plug.
-What is the trick?

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.300
-Now, now, now,
if you guess the bottle --

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.601
if you guess the price
of the bottle right,

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:16.434
you get to come and stay
at the house whenever you want,

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:17.734
back in your own house,
if you guess the bottle.

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:18.834
So how much do you think
this bottle is?

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:20.200
One bottle.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.501
-That's a nice bottle
of Prosecco.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:25.067
-How much do you think it is?
-I'm gonna say that's...

00:08:25.067 --> 00:08:27.667
a hundred...

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:29.767
$150 -- $175.

00:08:29.767 --> 00:08:31.567
-Okay, so check on the back.

00:08:31.567 --> 00:08:35.167
There should be a price,
like, on the barcode.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:37.234
There's a barcode on the back.

00:08:37.234 --> 00:08:38.901
What does it say?
Want to read it up close?

00:08:38.901 --> 00:08:40.667
-I'm looking at it right now,
but I want the audience to look.

